body: |-
  RESTART HERE for this arc. Branch conductor-revival-phase0, NOT merged (Matt merges/publishes himself). Launch /Applications/Conductor.app (build 701), ⌘⇧A.

  WHAT SHIPPED (the founder's "agents utilize the symbol graph by default, visually"):
  - Phase 1 (3d858e0b): #graph-slice-projector in @a-company/premise-core. `paradigm graph slice <symbol> [--radius N] [--mode ego|ripple|flow] [--format mermaid|envelope|json] [--as-lightbox]` + paradigm_graph_slice MCP tool. Sources edges from the LIVE parse (aggregateFromDirectory+buildSymbolIndex+getReferencesTo/From+flow membership — the ripple path), NOT the stale serialized indices. Deterministic topology, freshness stamp, fail-loud did-you-mean. 18 tests.
  - Phase 2a (d256fa93): native .graph VisualKind — AtriumGraphView (Canvas + ring layout, symbol-typed nodes, focus halo). FencedBlockParser.decodeGraph decodes the real envelope.
  - Phase 2b+2c (5689fb70): AgentDecision.symbols[] + DecisionOption.affectedSymbols[]; SessionPrompt "GROUND IN THE LIVE GRAPH" default-graph convention (render-by-projection, two-gate discriminator); hover an option row → spotlight its symbols / dim the rest (hoveredSymbols lifted to AtriumThreadView, kept OUT of Equatable AgentVisual).
  - Phase 2d (cabcc486): #decision-divergence-journal — Loid's falsifiable instrument. Grounded+diverged decisions (and agreements as denominator, + reopen watchdog) → ~/.paradigm/conductor/decisions/<session>.jsonl. PRODUCER only.

  NEXT / OPEN:
  - Manual test pass: .paradigm/research/graph-substrate-manual-test-checklist.md (Matt's list; nothing checked yet).
  - Deferred: T-2026-06-18-001 — learning CONSUMER (divergence rows → symbol-keyed notebook priors + paradigm doctor divergence/liveness metric; build on divergences only; keep separate from the token-cost grid).
  - Index-integrity debts surfaced: T-2026-06-13-011 (scan-index non-deterministic serialization; .purpose ': ' YAML breakage) + T-2026-06-17-008 (conductor flows missing from flow-index.json — context-field schema errors). Projector unaffected (live parse); other index consumers are not.
  - Pre-existing: merge conductor-revival-phase0; version bump + CHANGELOG release entry deferred to merge time (branch convention — Conductor commits don't bump).

  DISCIPLINE: Swift ecosystem agent owns ALL Conductor Swift; debug via ~/.paradigm/conductor/atrium transcripts; run the bundled .app; no blockquotes; be concise.
